    "blogtextliquid_ra7Awx": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>The secret behind modern gourmands is counterpoint. A master perfumer never pairs sweet notes with more sweetness; they balance roasted vanilla with dry cedar, salted caramel with bitter espresso, and praline with smoky incense.</p><p>This tension between dessert-like pleasure and austere woodiness creates scents that feel rich, confident, and endlessly compelling. Here is how sweet fragrances became the most sought-after category in luxury perfumery.</p>"
      }
    },
    "blocks_ji7beH": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "blog_editorial_text_section_zNd6WG": {
          "type": "blog--editorial-text-section",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Sugary High-Street Sprays vs Elevated Modern Gourmands",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_size_mobile": 28,
            "heading_line_height": 1.1,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 30,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 25,
            "column_1_text": "<p>Traditional teen gourmands relied heavily on cheap ethyl maltol—a synthetic compound that smells purely of spun sugar and caramelized syrup. Unanchored by woods or spices, these scents projected with loud, one-dimensional intensity.</p><p>They were fun for an afternoon at the beach, but lacked the refinement, elegance, and nuance required for dinner dates or professional environments.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>Modern luxury gourmands take a completely different architectural approach. They use dark Madagascar vanilla beans, bitter almond, roasted coffee, and tonka bean, supported by resinous amberwood and smoky vetiver.</p><p>The sweetness is not aggressive; it acts as a smooth, creamy glaze over deeply sophisticated base notes that bloom as your skin warms.</p>",
            "body_size": 17,
            "body_size_mobile": 15,
            "body_line_height": 1.9,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 55,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "blog_editorial_text_section_zNd6WG"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial text section",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "1778690749e24fd023": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "blog_narrative_content_9nTtAA": {
          "type": "blog--narrative-content",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "section_padding": 60,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "heading": "<p>The unisex crossover: Silk Odyssey & Feminine Fancy</p>",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_spacing": 25,
            "box_color": "#1C1917",
            "box_radius": 15,
            "box_padding": 45,
            "box_spacing": 35,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>One of the most exciting developments in modern fragrance is that men have discovered gourmands. Sweetness is no longer gendered. Accords of bourbon vanilla, roasted hazelnut, and dark rum create an unforgettable masculine evening aura.</p><p><strong>Silk Odyssey</strong> (inspired by Oud Satin Mood by Maison Francis Kurkdjian) pairs decadent Turkish rose and violet with rich vanilla and dark Laotian oud, creating a velvet-textured masterpiece that commands respect.</p><p>Meanwhile, <strong>Feminine Fancy</strong> (inspired by Good Girl) blends roasted tonka bean with white jasmine and cocoa for an intoxicating café-vibe sillage.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#F5EFE6",
            "box_text_size": 17,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.9,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "subheading": "<p>How to wear gourmands without overwhelming the room</p>",
            "subheading_size": 42,
            "subheading_color": "#1A1816",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>Because gourmand molecules are dense and long-lasting, a little goes a very long way. Two sprays on pulse points under your clothing are enough to create a warm, inviting scent bubble.</p><p>They shine brightest in cooler British temperatures—autumn breezes, winter evenings, and cozy pub settings bring out their creamy decadence without cloying.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 17,
            "bottom_text_color": "#2D2A26",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.9
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "blog_narrative_content_9nTtAA"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
