        "blog_editorial_callout_section_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "blog--editorial-callout-section",
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1100,
            "left_column_width": 45,
            "right_column_width": 55,
            "column_gap": 50,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "What this means when you are shopping",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "mobile_heading_size": 28,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_indent": 0,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 0,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Work_with_your_own_skin_not_a_stranger_s_jpg.jpg",
            "image_max_width": 500,
            "heading_image_gap": 16,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 20,
            "body_text": "<p>When testing a gourmand fragrance, give it time to settle through the initial sweetness. The opening 5 minutes will always highlight the top notes, but the true magic happens after 30 minutes when the woods, spices, and musks emerge.</p><p>Look for balanced formulations that feel like an organic extension of your personal style rather than a bakery counter.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
